    <h1>Residential treatment</h1>
    <p class="lede">Detox is about getting safe. Residential is where there is enough time — and enough distance from daily triggers — to look at what is underneath.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p>Clients live on campus: a bed, shared common spaces, a structured day, and a peer community. Individual therapy, daily groups (CBT, skills, process, psychoeducation), family work when timed correctly, psychiatric care, and aftercare planning that starts early.</p>
    <p>Length of stay is clinical, not a brochure number. Insurance authorization and progress both matter. We will not promise “30, 60, or 90” as a product. We will advocate for the time that is medically necessary.</p>
    <p>The URL <a href="/programs/inpatient/">/programs/inpatient/</a> redirects here. In our licensing and in California practice, the live-in program after detox is residential treatment.</p>
  </div></section>
